G4128.def:
πλῆθος, -ους, τό 
[in LXX chiefly for רֹב, also for הָמוֹן, etc. ;] 
__1. a great number, a multitude; 
__(a) of things : ἰχθύων, Luc 5:6, Jean 21:6; φρυγάνων, Actes 28:3; ἁμαρτιίῶν, Jacques 5:20, 1 Pierre 4:8; τ. πλήθει, in multitude, Hébreux 11:12; 
__(b) of persons: Actes 21:22 (WH, R, om.); with genitive, Luc 2:13, Jean 5:3, Actes 5:14; π. πολύ (πολὺ π.), Marc 3:7-8; id. with genitive, Luc 6:17 23:27, Actes 14:1 17:4 
__2. Of persons, with art., the whole number, the multitude (in Plat., Thuc., Xen., al., = δῆμος, the commons, or-opposite to δῆμος-the populace) : Actes 2:6 15:30 19:9 23:7; τ. λαοῦ, Actes 21:36; τ. πόλεως, Actes 14:4; πᾶν τὸ π., Actes 15:12; with genitive, Luc 1:10 8:37 19:37 23:1, Actes 4:32 5:16 6:2, 5 25:24.†

G4137.def:
πληρόω, -ῶ 
[in LXX chiefly for מָלֵא ;] 
__1. to fill, make full, fill to the full, with accusative; 
__(a) of things : pass. (σαψήνη, φάραγξ), Matthieu 13:48, Luc 3:5" (LXX) ; figuratively, Matthieu 23:32; but chiefly of immaterial things: πᾶσαν χρείαν, Philippiens 4:19; ἦχος ἐλήρωσε τ. οἶκον, Actes 2:2; with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), Actes 5:28; pass., before ἐκ, Jean 12:3 (cf. B1., § 36, 4); π. τ. καρδίαν, Jean 16:6, Actes 5:3; metaphorically, of the all-pervading activity of Christ, Éphésiens 4:10; mid., Éphésiens 1:23; 
__(b) of persons: to fill with, cause to abound in : with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), Actes 2:28 (LXX), Romains 15:13; pass., to be filled with, abound in: Éphésiens 3:19, Philippiens 4:18; with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), Actes 13:52, Romains 15:14, 2 Timothée 1:4; with dative (Æsch., al.), Luc 2:40 (with genitive, T), Romains 1:29, 2 Corinthiens 7:4; with accusative (so in π., see MM, xx), Philippiens 1:11, Colossiens 1:9; before ἐν, Éphésiens 5:18, Colossiens 2:10. 
__2. to complete; 
__(a) to complete, fulfil: of number, Apocalypse 6:11, WH, tat.; of time (MM, xx), Marc 1:15, Luc 21:24, Jean 7:8, Actes 7:23, 30 9:23 24:27; ἐυδοκίαν, 2 Thessaloniciens 1:11; τ. χαράν, Philippiens 2:2; pass., Jean 3:29 15:11 16:24 17:13, 1 Jean 1:4, 2Jn.12; τ. ἔργα, Apocalypse 3:2; ἡ ὑπακυή, 2 Corinthiens 10:6; τ. πάσχα, Luc 22:16; 
__(b) to execute, accomplish, carry out to the full: Matthieu 3:15, Luc 7:1 9:31, Actes 12:25 13:25 14:26 19:21, Romains 8:4 13:8 15:19, Galates 5:14, Colossiens 1:25 4:17, Apocalypse 6:11, T, WH, R, mg.; 
__(with) of sayings, prophecies, etc., to bring to pass, fulfil: Matthieu 1:22 2:15, 17 2:23 4:14 5:17 8:17 12:17 13:35 21:4 26:54, 56 27:9, Marc 14:49 15:28 (WH, R, txt. om.), Luc 1:20 4:21 24:44, Jean 12:38 13:18 15:25 17:12 18:9, 32 19:24, 36, Actes 1:16 3:18 13:27, Jacques 2:23 (cf. Lft., Col., 255 ff.).†

G4152.def:
πνευματικός, -ή, -όν
(πνεῦμα), 
__1. of or caused by the wind, air or breath (Arist., al.). 
__2. spiritual (opposite to σωματικός, Plut.); 
__(a) of created beings : τὰ π. (RV, the spiritual hosts), Éphésiens 6:12; of that which is related to the human spirit, opposite to ψυχικός, 1 Corinthiens 15:44 15:46; 
__(b) of that which belongs to or is actuated by the Divine Spirit; 
__α of persons : 1 Corinthiens 2:15 3:1 14:37, Galates 6:1; οἶκος π., figuratively, 1 Pierre 2:5; 
__β of things : Romains 1:11 7:14, 1 Corinthiens 2:13 10:3-4 12:1 14:1, Éphésiens 1:3 5:19, Colossiens 1:9 3:16, 1 Pierre 2:5; opposite to τ. σαρκικά, Romains 15:27, 1 Corinthiens 9:11.†
SYN.: ψυχικός, which see, and cf. DB, ii, 410, iv, 612

G4153.def:
πνευματικῶς 
adv. (πνεῦμα), 
spiritually; 
__(a) by the aid of the Holy Spirit: 1 Corinthiens 2:13 (WH, mg.), 1 Corinthiens 2:14; 
__(b) in a spiritual sense : Apocalypse 11:8.†

G4159.def:
πόθεν 
adv., 
whence; 
__(a) of place: Matthieu 15:33, Luc 13:25, 27, Jean 3:8 6:5 8:14 9:29-30 19:9, Apocalypse 7:13; metaphorically, of condition, Apocalypse 2:5; 
__(b) of origin: Matthieu 13:27, 54 13:56 21:25, Marc 6:2, Luc 20:7, Jean 2:9, Jacques 4:1; of parentage, Jean 7:27-28; 
__(with) of cause: Marc 8:4 12:37, Luc 1:43, Jean 1:49 4:11.†

G4169.def:
ποῖος, -α, -ον 
interrog. pronom. adj. (corresponding to the demonstr. τοῖος and the relat. οἷος), [in LXX chiefly for זֶה אֵי־ ;] 
of what quality or sort: absol., n. pl., Luc 24:19; with subst.; 
__(a) prop., in direct questions: Matthieu 19:18 21:23 22:36 24:42, Marc 11:28 12:28, Luc 6:32-34, Jean 10:32, Actes 4:7 7:49, Romains 3:27, 1 Corinthiens 15:35, Jacques 4:14 (but see: ποία), 1 Pierre 2:20; 
__(b) in indirect questions = ὁποῖος : Matthieu 21:24, 27 24:43, Marc 11:29, 33, Luc 12:39 20:2, 8, Jean 12:33 18:32 21:19 Actes 23:34, 1 Pierre 1:11, Apocalypse 3:3; ποῖας (sc. ὁδοῦ), Luc 5:19.†

G4190.def:
πονηρός, -ά, -όν
(πονέω, to toil), [in LXX chiefly for רַע ;] 
__1. 
__(a) of persons, oppressed by toils (Hes.); 
__(b) of things, toilsome, painful (καιρός, Sir.51:12): Éphésiens 5:16 6:13 Apocalypse 16:2. 
__2. bad, worthless; 
__(a) in physical sense: καρπός, Matthieu 7:17-18; 
__(b) in ethical sense, bad, evil, wicked; 
__(α) of persons: Matthieu 7:11 12:34-35 18:32 25:26, Luc 6:45 11:13 19:22, Actes 17:5, 2 Thessaloniciens 3:2, 2 Timothée 3:13; γενεά, Matthieu 12:39, 45 16:4, Luc 11:29; πνεῦμια, Matthieu 12:45, Luc 7:21 8:2 11:26, Actes 19:12-13, 15-16; as subst., οἱ π., opposite to δίκαιοι, Matthieu 13:49; to ἀγαθοί, Matthieu 5:45 22:10; οἱ ἀχάριστοι καὶ π., Luc 6:35; sing., ὁ π., Matthieu 5:39, 1 Corinthiens 5:13; id. esp. of Satan, the evil one, Matthieu 5:37 6:13 (see Lft., Notes, 125 ff.; but cf. McN, in l) Matthieu 13:19, 38, Luc 11:4 (WH, R, om.), Jean 17:15, Éphésiens 6:16, 2 Thessaloniciens 3:3 (Lft., Notes, l.with), 1 Jean 2:13-14 Jn 3:12 Jn 5:18-19; 
__(β) of things: Matthieu 5:11 12:35 15:19, Luc 6:22, 45, Jean 3:19 7:7, Actes 18:14 25:18, Galates 1:4, Colossiens 1:21, 1 Timothée 6:4, 2 Timothée 4:18, Hébreux 3:12 10:22, Jacques 2:4 4:16, 1 Jean 3:12, II Jn 11, 3Jn.10; ὀφθαλμός (which see), Matthieu 6:23 20:15, Marc 7:22, Luc 11:34; as subst., neut., τὸ π., Actes 28:21, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:22; opposite to ἀγαθόν, Luc 6:45, Romains 12:9; pl., Matthieu 9:4, Marc 7:23, Luc 3:19.
† SYN.: see: ἄθεσμος

G4198.def:
πορεύω, 
(πόρος, a ford, a passage), [in LXX chiefly for הלךְ ;] 
in cl. (the act. becomes obsolete in late Gk.; see M, Pr., 162), to cause to go over, carry, convey. Mid. (always in LXX and NT), ־ομαι, to go, proceed, go on one's way: with accusative, ὁδόν, Actes 8:39; before ἐκεῖθεν, Matthieu 19:15; ἐντεῦθεν, Luc 13:31; ἀπό, Matthieu 25:41, Luc 4:42; εἰς, Matthieu 2:20, Marc 16:12, Luc 1:39, Jean 7:35, al; εἰς εἰρήνην (cf. 1 Rois 1:17). Luc 7:50; ἐν εἰρήνῃ, Actes 16:36; ἐπί, with accusative, Matthieu 22:9, Actes 25:12, al; ἕως, Actes 23:23; οὗ, Luc 24:28, 1 Corinthiens 16:6; πρός, with accusative of person(s), Matthieu 25:9, Luc 11:5, al.; κατὰ τ. ὁδόν, Actes 8:36; διά, with genitive, Matthieu 12:1, Marc 9:30; with inf., Luc 2:3, Jean 14:2; σύν, Luc 7:6, al.; ἵνα, Jean 11:11; absol., Matthieu 2:9, Luc 7:8, Jean 4:50, Actes 5:20, al.; ptcp., πορευθείς (on the pass. form of the aor., see M, Pr., 161f.), redundant (as in Heb. and Aram.; V. M, Pr., 231; Dalman, Words, 21), Matthieu 2:8, Luc 7:22, al. Metaphorical (cf. Soph., O.T., 884; Xen., Cyr., 2, 2, 24, al), 
__(a) like οἴχομαι in cl., as euphemism for θνήσκω (so הלךְ in Genèse 15:2); Luc 22:22 and perh. also 13:33 (see Field, Notes, 66); 
__(b) in ethical sense (Deutéronome 19:9, Psaumes 14:2, al; cf. M, Pr., 11.2; Kennedy, Sources, 107): before ἐν, Luc 1:6, 1 Pierre 4:3, 2 Pierre 2:19; κατά, with accusative, 2 Pierre 3:3, Ju 16, 18; with dative (Bl, §38, 3), Actes 9:31 14:16, Ju 11; 
__(with) of disciples or partisans ( Juges 2:12, 3Ki.11:10, Sir.46:10): before ὀπίσω, with genitive of person(s), Luc 21:8 (cf. δια-, εἰς-, (-μαι), ἐκ- (-μαι), ἐν- (-μαι), ἐπι- (-μαι), παρα- (-μαι), προ-, προσ- (-μαι), συν- (-μαι)).
